  "strategy": "enlist sacrifice damage-cannon aggro",
  "colors": "RG",
  "identity": "A red aggro deck whose distinguishing reach is a two-card damage cannon. REVISED AFTER THE GRILL: the Berserker-plus-outlet line below is the deck's CEILING, not its baseline - it needs one of 2 projector copies AND one of 3 outlet copies simultaneously, which assembles in 37.7% of games by turn 6 (P(projector) 0.550 x P(outlet) 0.704, hypergeometric over 13 cards seen). Below that line the deck is a 16-creature red aggro list with menace, trample and flying, closing on 6 copies of any-target damage. The distinguishing line, when it does assemble, uses enlist as a loading mechanism rather than as a combat trick. Balduvian Berserker reads 'Enlist ... / When this creature dies, it deals damage equal to its power to any target.' Enlist inflates its power as it attacks, and a sacrifice outlet then fires that inflated number at ANY TARGET - so blockers are irrelevant and the deck kills through a board stall that the pure combat builds of this archetype cannot break. The cleanest line uses one card twice: Balduvian Berserker attacks and enlists Hurler Cyclops (a 5/4), becoming a 6/3; because the Cyclops' ability reads '{1}, Sacrifice another creature' with NO tap symbol in its cost, that same freshly-tapped Cyclops then eats the Berserker for {1}, dealing 6 to the face plus its own 1.",
